  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 1.2. Increased institutional capacity of workers&#x2019; organizations</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Confederation of Ethiopian Trade Unions (CETU) adopted a 3-year action plan (2022-2025) covering a series of priority policy areas to tackle poverty, decent work deficits and climate change-induced calamities. 

CETU organized 40,000 new members, established joint labour-management OHS committees, signed collective bargaining agreements in several workplaces, and provided assistance that enabled 42 domestic workers&#x2019; associations to sign contracts covering 6,000 domestic workers and their employees.  

CETU launched the Migrant Recruitment Advisor in November 2022, which is a valuable tool for not only raising awareness but also for protecting migrant workers.

CETU revised in June 2022 its draft national policy on child labour by incorporating ILO&#x2019;s approaches and standards on forced labour and human trafficking. It also developed a Manual and a Trainer&#x2019;s Guide on Forced Labour and Human Trafficking.  

CETU  improved  the inclusion of underrepresented groups in its decision making bodies, and boosted its accessibility and service delivery capacity. 

CETU mobilized its members to participate in the national tree planting effort dubbed as Ethiopia&#x2019;s Tree Planting Legacy Initiative, which is contributing to carbon sinking, afforestation, land reclamation, landscaping, job creation and improved livelihoods. ILO organized several workshops for the CETU on union organizing and revitalization, labour migration, child labour, etc., using RBTC funds and resources from the Better Regional Migration Management (BRMM) Project, the Towards SDG Target 8.7 project and the German Federal Ministry of Labour and Social Affairs (BMAS) project and the ProAgro project.</narrative>
   </description>
   <document-link format="TEXT/HTML" url="https://www.ilo.org/IRDashboard/">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">The ILO&#x2019;s Decent Work Results Dashboard</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
